WEBVTT

00:00:00.438 --> 00:00:03.411
This is Autopilot, a test automation platform.

00:00:03.411 --> 00:00:06.281
In the next few minutes we'll go end to end:

00:00:06.281 --> 00:00:11.151
write a test in plain English, run it on Playwright and Selenium, replay the script

00:00:11.151 --> 00:00:15.662
it generates, design test cases from a user story, and run everything across

00:00:15.662 --> 00:00:16.738
machines.

00:00:17.638 --> 00:00:20.005
Everything happens in the web app.

00:00:20.005 --> 00:00:24.790
After signing in, the overview shows the pass rate, what needs attention, what is

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.208
running right now, and recent runs.

00:00:28.108 --> 00:00:32.736
In Studio, we describe a test the way we would explain it to a colleague.

00:00:32.736 --> 00:00:34.751
No code and no selectors.

00:00:34.751 --> 00:00:39.924
Open the shop, search for a wireless mouse, open the first Logitech result, add two

00:00:39.924 --> 00:00:42.538
to the cart, and check the subtotal.

00:00:43.438 --> 00:00:47.047
Break down into steps shows exactly how it was understood:

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:51.740
one action per step, the element described in words, and the value it will use.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:54.318
You can edit the steps before running.

00:00:55.218 --> 00:00:56.532
Now we run it.

00:00:56.532 --> 00:00:59.110
The browser streams into the page live.

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:03.658
Each element is found on the live page, outlined in green, and acted on with a

00:01:03.658 --> 00:01:05.579
native Playwright locator.

00:01:05.579 --> 00:01:09.218
Every step gets a screenshot, and the locator that found it.

00:01:10.118 --> 00:01:12.159
Every run has its own page.

00:01:12.159 --> 00:01:14.514
The steps with their screenshots.

00:01:14.514 --> 00:01:16.188
The video recording.

00:01:16.188 --> 00:01:20.636
The generated Playwright and Selenium scripts, with the whole run folder.

00:01:20.636 --> 00:01:22.625
A single file HTML report.

00:01:22.625 --> 00:01:25.398
And the data and settings that were used.

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:30.373
Replay runs the generated script in script mode.

00:01:30.373 --> 00:01:35.206
There is no parsing and no AI, just the stored native locators, so it is fast.

00:01:35.206 --> 00:01:40.255
If the page has changed and a locator breaks, the engine heals it and writes a new

00:01:40.255 --> 00:01:41.276
script.

00:01:41.276 --> 00:01:43.800
Here we replay on Selenium instead.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.520
Tests are data driven.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:51.500
Placeholders in the test take their values from a grid, one row per run, and each

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:53.642
row can use its own browser.

00:01:53.642 --> 00:01:58.461
We choose both engines, and share the work between the hub and a remote agent.

00:01:58.461 --> 00:02:00.870
One click, four runs in parallel.

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:04.382
Autopilot can also write the tests.

00:02:04.382 --> 00:02:07.383
Paste a user story, or pick one from Jira.

00:02:07.383 --> 00:02:12.717
It reads the acceptance criteria and the code behind them, here a Git commit for the

00:02:12.717 --> 00:02:17.941
sign up form, and designs positive, negative and boundary cases, with rules alone.

00:02:17.941 --> 00:02:19.330
No AI needed.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:23.172
All thirteen cases were approved and run.

00:02:23.172 --> 00:02:24.448
One failed.

00:02:24.448 --> 00:02:29.721
The form accepts an age of one hundred, but the story says eighteen to ninety nine.

00:02:29.721 --> 00:02:34.772
The run shows the failing step, what was expected, and the page at that moment.

00:02:34.772 --> 00:02:39.990
Results can go back to Zephyr, Xray and Jira, including a bug with the screenshot.

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:43.316
Tests run wherever you need them.

00:02:43.316 --> 00:02:48.490
The hub runs tests itself, and any Windows, Mac, Linux or Docker machine joins as an

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:51.347
agent with one command and its own token.

00:02:51.347 --> 00:02:55.282
Agents connect out to the hub, so they work behind firewalls.

00:02:55.282 --> 00:02:58.840
Cloud grids such as BrowserStack plug in the same way.

00:02:59.741 --> 00:03:04.930
For teams, there are accounts and roles, company single sign on, projects that keep

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:10.065
each team's work apart, tokens for Jira, GitHub and test tools, and the AI of your

00:03:10.065 --> 00:03:11.103
choice:

00:03:11.103 --> 00:03:15.691
your Claude, Copilot or Cursor subscription, an API key, or none at all.

00:03:19.596 --> 00:03:22.362
Everything Autopilot produces is yours.

00:03:22.362 --> 00:03:25.073
Plain Playwright and Selenium scripts.

00:03:25.073 --> 00:03:28.761
An exported project that runs in any CI without the hub.

00:03:28.761 --> 00:03:32.665
And every result in a SQLite database, with reporting views.

00:03:32.665 --> 00:03:37.166
Set it up with one command, and find the full guide in the docs folder.

